IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `eia-core`
IMPORT `eia-core-interpretation`
IMPORT `ei4-parts-viii-viii3`

-- Tests of ei4-parts-viii-viii3.l4 (Act ss 153 to 153.4). Expected values are written by hand from the text of the section; none is
-- copied from the module's output. Days of the week are worked on a calendar: 12 March 2022 was a Saturday (1 January 2022 was a
-- Saturday, so 1 March was a Tuesday and 12 March a Saturday).

§ `s 153(9) -- sitting day`

#ASSERT `s 153(9) the day is a sitting day` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `s 153(9) the day is a sitting day` FALSE

§ `s 153.1 -- the class for the alternate access scheme`

-- 153.1(1): an insured person with 600 hours in the qualifying period who does not qualify under section 7: in the class.
#ASSERT `s 153.1(1) the person is in the class for whom the scheme is made` TRUE 600 FALSE
-- 153.1(1): 599 hours is below "at least 600".
#ASSERT NOT `s 153.1(1) the person is in the class for whom the scheme is made` TRUE 599 FALSE
-- 153.1(1): more than 600 hours is still "at least 600".
#ASSERT `s 153.1(1) the person is in the class for whom the scheme is made` TRUE 700 FALSE
-- 153.1(1): a person who does qualify under section 7 is not in the class.
#ASSERT NOT `s 153.1(1) the person is in the class for whom the scheme is made` TRUE 700 TRUE
-- 153.1(1): not an insured person.
#ASSERT NOT `s 153.1(1) the person is in the class for whom the scheme is made` FALSE 700 FALSE
-- 153.1(3): subject to an increase under section 7.1: the scheme may not provide special benefits.
#ASSERT `s 153.1(3) the scheme may not provide special benefits to the person` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `s 153.1(3) the scheme may not provide special benefits to the person` FALSE
-- 153.1(1) and (3): in the class and not subject to an increase: the scheme is meant to give special benefits.
#ASSERT `s 153.1 the scheme is meant to give the person special benefits` TRUE 600 FALSE FALSE
-- 153.1(3): in the class but subject to a section 7.1 increase: excluded.
#ASSERT NOT `s 153.1 the scheme is meant to give the person special benefits` TRUE 600 FALSE TRUE
-- 153.1(1): 599 hours: not in the class.
#ASSERT NOT `s 153.1 the scheme is meant to give the person special benefits` TRUE 599 FALSE FALSE

§ `s 153.3 -- when an interim order may be made`

-- 153.3(9): the power is not exercised after September 30, 2020.
#ASSERT `s 153.3(9) September 30, 2020` EQUALS YMD 2020 9 30
-- 153.3(1): made to mitigate the economic effects of COVID-19 and adding, adapting or disapplying provisions.
#ASSERT `s 153.3(1) the order is an interim order of the kind the Minister may make` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `s 153.3(1) the order is an interim order of the kind the Minister may make` FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `s 153.3(1) the order is an interim order of the kind the Minister may make` TRUE FALSE
-- 153.3(2): not in respect of Part IV or VII, nor of a regulation made for those Parts.
#ASSERT `s 153.3(2) an interim order is not to be made in respect of the matter` TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT `s 153.3(2) an interim order is not to be made in respect of the matter` FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `s 153.3(2) an interim order is not to be made in respect of the matter` FALSE FALSE
-- 153.3(3): the Minister of Finance's consent is needed; (4): for Part III, the President of the Treasury Board's as well.
#ASSERT `s 153.3(3) and (4) the consents required for the order have been given` TRUE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT `s 153.3(3) and (4) the consents required for the order have been given` TRUE TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `s 153.3(3) and (4) the consents required for the order have been given` TRUE TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `s 153.3(3) and (4) the consents required for the order have been given` FALSE FALSE TRUE
-- 153.3: a valid order made on the last day of the power (30 September 2020).
#ASSERT `s 153.3 an interim order may be made` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE (YMD 2020 9 30)
-- 153.3(9): one day later is too late.
#ASSERT NOT `s 153.3 an interim order may be made` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE (YMD 2020 10 1)
-- 153.3(2): an order in respect of Part VII cannot be made.
#ASSERT NOT `s 153.3 an interim order may be made` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE (YMD 2020 6 1)
#ASSERT NOT `s 153.3 an interim order may be made` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE (YMD 2020 6 1)
-- 153.3(3): without the Minister of Finance's consent.
#ASSERT NOT `s 153.3 an interim order may be made` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE (YMD 2020 6 1)
-- 153.3(4): an order in respect of Part III needs the President of the Treasury Board too.
#ASSERT NOT `s 153.3 an interim order may be made` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE (YMD 2020 6 1)
#ASSERT `s 153.3 an interim order may be made` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE (YMD 2020 6 1)
-- 153.3(1): not made for the COVID-19 purpose.
#ASSERT NOT `s 153.3 an interim order may be made` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE (YMD 2020 6 1)

§ `s 153.3(6) to (8) -- retroactive effect, cessation, conflict`

-- 153.3(6): an interim order may have retroactive effect if it so provides.
#ASSERT `s 153.3(6) the interim order has retroactive effect` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `s 153.3(6) the interim order has retroactive effect` FALSE
-- 153.3(7)(c): takes effect on Monday 15 March 2021; the first anniversary is Tuesday 15 March 2022; the Saturday after is 19 March 2022.
#ASSERT `s 153.3(7)(c) the Saturday after the first anniversary of the day on which the interim order takes effect` (YMD 2021 3 15) EQUALS YMD 2022 3 19
-- 153.3(7)(c): the first anniversary is Friday 11 March 2022; the Saturday after is the next day, 12 March.
#ASSERT `s 153.3(7)(c) the Saturday after the first anniversary of the day on which the interim order takes effect` (YMD 2021 3 11) EQUALS YMD 2022 3 12
-- 153.3(7)(c): the first anniversary is itself a Saturday (12 March 2022): "the Saturday after" is strictly after, so 19 March (fork F-ei4-17).
#ASSERT `s 153.3(7)(c) the Saturday after the first anniversary of the day on which the interim order takes effect` (YMD 2021 3 12) EQUALS YMD 2022 3 19
-- 153.3(7)(c): the first anniversary is Sunday 13 March 2022: the Saturday after is 19 March.
#ASSERT `s 153.3(7)(c) the Saturday after the first anniversary of the day on which the interim order takes effect` (YMD 2021 3 13) EQUALS YMD 2022 3 19
-- 153.3(7)(c): an order taking effect on 29 February 2020 has no first anniversary on 29 February; the keel's `add years` gives 28 February 2021 (a Sunday), and the Saturday after is 6 March 2021.
#ASSERT `s 153.3(7)(c) the Saturday after the first anniversary of the day on which the interim order takes effect` (YMD 2020 2 29) EQUALS YMD 2021 3 6
-- 153.3(7): the earliest of (a) 30 June 2021, (b) none, (c) 19 March 2022 is 30 June 2021.
#ASSERT `s 153.3(7) the day on which the added provisions, adaptations and non-application provisions must cease to apply` (JUST (YMD 2021 6 30)) NOTHING (YMD 2021 3 15) EQUALS YMD 2021 6 30
-- 153.3(7): repealed on 1 May 2021, before the day specified (30 June 2021): 1 May 2021.
#ASSERT `s 153.3(7) the day on which the added provisions, adaptations and non-application provisions must cease to apply` (JUST (YMD 2021 6 30)) (JUST (YMD 2021 5 1)) (YMD 2021 3 15) EQUALS YMD 2021 5 1
-- 153.3(7): nothing specified and not repealed: the Saturday after the first anniversary.
#ASSERT `s 153.3(7) the day on which the added provisions, adaptations and non-application provisions must cease to apply` NOTHING NOTHING (YMD 2021 3 15) EQUALS YMD 2022 3 19
-- 153.3(7): a specified day later than the Saturday after the first anniversary does not extend it.
#ASSERT `s 153.3(7) the day on which the added provisions, adaptations and non-application provisions must cease to apply` (JUST (YMD 2023 1 1)) NOTHING (YMD 2021 3 15) EQUALS YMD 2022 3 19
-- 153.3(7): repealed on the very day of (c): the same day.
#ASSERT `s 153.3(7) the day on which the added provisions, adaptations and non-application provisions must cease to apply` NOTHING (JUST (YMD 2022 3 19)) (YMD 2021 3 15) EQUALS YMD 2022 3 19
-- the helper: the earlier of two days.
#ASSERT `s 153.3(7) the earlier of two days` (YMD 2021 1 1) (YMD 2021 1 2) EQUALS YMD 2021 1 1
#ASSERT `s 153.3(7) the earlier of two days` (YMD 2021 1 2) (YMD 2021 1 1) EQUALS YMD 2021 1 1
-- 153.3(8): an order that applies despite the Act prevails where it conflicts.
#ASSERT `s 153.3(8) the interim order or added provision prevails to the extent that it conflicts with this Act or a regulation` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `s 153.3(8) the interim order or added provision prevails to the extent that it conflicts with this Act or a regulation` TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `s 153.3(8) the interim order or added provision prevails to the extent that it conflicts with this Act or a regulation` FALSE TRUE
